{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"serverInfo":{"name":"petmcp","version":"devel"},"instructions":"PetMcp emulates the Commodore PET 3032 with an SD2PET disk drive on its IEEE-488 bus. emu_status says what runs. Integers may be written as hex strings, \"0x1000\" or \"$1000\". The tools are the methods of docs/spec/control-protocol.md."}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"audio_capture_start","description":"Keeps the PET's sound from now on, every run's, until audio.capture_stop writes it: stereo at 48 kHz, CB2 on both channels, the expansion board's AY1 on the left and AY2 on the right.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"audio_capture_stop","description":"Ends the capture, and writes what it kept to path as a WAV: 16-bit stereo at 48 kHz.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the WAV."}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"cpu_disassemble","description":"Disassembles instructions as the 6502 would read them, without the side effects of reading; undocumented opcodes are marked with a star.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"Where to start."},"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many instructions, at most 1000."}},"required":["address","count"]}},{"name":"cpu_get_state","description":"The 6502's registers at the instruction boundary the PET stands at, the instruction there, and the cycle it begins in.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_add","description":"Stops runs before the instruction at an address. The instruction the PET stands at runs when it runs on.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The instruction's address."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_list","description":"The breakpoints' addresses, ascending.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_remove","description":"Removes the breakpoint at an address.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The instruction's address."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_trace","description":"The history of execution, counted back from now: index 0 is the newest instruction, the one the PET stands at, 1 the one that ran before it, and so on, over the last seconds debug.trace.configure sets. Answers count of them from index from, newest first, each with the cycle it began in, the registers before it, and its bytes and disassembly as they were when it ran.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many, 0 to 4096; 32 when left out."},"from":{"type":"integer","description":"The newest one's index, 0 being the newest kept; 0 when left out."}}}},{"name":"debug_trace_configure","description":"How many seconds of the PET's time the history of execution keeps, 0.01 to 60, from now and after every power-up. A second is some 300,000 instructions, 5 MB.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"seconds":{"type":"number","description":"The history's length."}},"required":["seconds"]}},{"name":"debug_trace_find","description":"Searches the history of execution back from index from, 0 being the newest, for instructions that meet every condition given, and answers up to limit of them, newest first, as debug.trace does. next_from continues the search where it stopped, or is null when it reached the oldest.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pc":{"type":"integer","description":"The instruction's address."},"pc_start":{"type":"integer","description":"With pc_end: the instruction's address is at least this."},"pc_end":{"type":"integer","description":"With pc_start: the instruction's address is below this."},"disasm_contains":{"type":"string","description":"Its disassembly, as it ran, holds this text, case aside: STA $80, E812, JSR."},"a":{"type":"integer","description":"A before it."},"x":{"type":"integer","description":"X before it."},"y":{"type":"integer","description":"Y before it."},"s":{"type":"integer","description":"S before it."},"from":{"type":"integer","description":"The index to search back from; 0, the newest, when left out."},"limit":{"type":"integer","description":"The most matches to answer, 1 to 4096; 32 when left out."}}}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_add","description":"Stops runs after the instruction that reads or writes data in a range: any access of its own beyond fetching its bytes, dummy accesses included. One per address; a second replaces the first.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The range's first address."},"size":{"type":"integer","description":"Bytes in the range; 1 when left out."},"access":{"type":"string","description":"read, write (the default) or access for both."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_list","description":"The watchpoints, by address.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_remove","description":"Removes the watchpoint at an address.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The range's first address."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"disk_card","description":"Puts a host directory in the SD2PET as its SD card, for this PET and those powered up after it; an empty path takes the card out. The drive starts afresh at the card's root, as after a card change.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"The directory."}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"disk_command","description":"Runs a DOS command in the SD2PET as if the PET had sent it on channel 15 (CD:NAME, S:NAME, N:NAME,ID, U1 2 0 18 0 ...), at once and beside the bus, and answers the status it leaves. Letters of either case are sent as the PET's keyboard types them; ← (or _) is the left arrow.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"The command."}},"required":["command"]}},{"name":"disk_mount","description":"Enters a disk image (D64, D71, D81, D80, D82, DNP) in the SD2PET, wherever on the host it is, as CD of it would from its directory, which becomes the current one. Answers the drive, its status the one the mount left.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"The image file."}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"disk_run","description":"Runs a program from the SD2PET as a person would: enters the image given, if one is, waits for the PET's READY. after power-up, types LOAD\"name\",8 (the first file when no name is given), runs the PET until the load ends, and types RUN, which runs when the PET next runs. Fails with the screen's error when the load does.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"A disk image to enter first; the drive as it is when left out."},"file":{"type":"string","description":"The file to load; * (the first) when left out."}}}},{"name":"disk_status","description":"The SD2PET on the IEEE-488 port, device 8: the directory standing for its SD card, the directory current on it and the image entered there, as host paths, its device number, and its error channel's message as the PET would read it now, without reading it.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"disk_unmount","description":"Leaves the image entered in the SD2PET, as CD← does. Answers the drive.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_pause","description":"Pauses the PET where it runs by itself: in the desktop application, which then runs it only on request. petmcp-cli runs only on request anyway.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_reset","description":"Pulls the PET's reset line: the 6502, the PIAs and the VIA reset, RAM and the video run on. With power, switches it off and on instead: RAM as at power-up, the ROMs read again.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"power":{"type":"boolean","description":"Switch off and on rather than reset; false when left out."}}}},{"name":"emu_resume","description":"Lets the PET run by itself again, where it does: in the desktop application.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_run_cycles","description":"Runs cycles of the 1 MHz clock, and stops at the next instruction boundary.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Cycles to run at least."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_run_frames","description":"Runs through frame boundaries, where the vertical blank begins, 60.1 a second, and stops at the next instruction boundary.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Frame boundaries to run through."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_run_until","description":"Runs until a condition holds at an instruction boundary: the 6502 about to run the instruction at pc, or the screen showing a text. Give one or both; with both, either stops it.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pc":{"type":"integer","description":"Stop before the instruction at this address."},"screen_contains":{"type":"string","description":"Stop when the screen, as video.screen_text reads it, shows this text on one line."},"timeout_cycles":{"type":"integer","description":"Cycles after which to give up; 20,000,000 (20 s) when left out."}}}},{"name":"emu_set_rom_directory","description":"Reads the PET's ROMs from a directory from now on, under the names VICE gives them, and powers it up with them. On failure what ran runs on.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"The directory."}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"emu_status","description":"The emulator's version, whether the window's own run is paused, and the PET's time: cycles of its 1 MHz clock and frames since power-up; or, when it is not running, why.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_step","description":"Runs instructions, one when count is left out, stopping before at a breakpoint or after a watched access.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many instructions, 1 to 1,000,000."}}}},{"name":"expansion_get_state","description":"The expansion board: both YM2149Fs' registers and the register each one's latch selects, the RAM banks at $A000 and $B000, the characters the video draws, and the chips' clocks.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"ieee_trace","description":"The IEEE-488 port's changes, counted back from the newest: index 0 is the last change. Each gives its cycle, the byte on the data lines (a low line is a 1), the control lines low, and which of them the PET and the SD2PET each pull. The last 65536 changes are kept.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"How many, 0 to 4096; 64 when left out."},"from":{"type":"integer","description":"The newest one's index; 0 when left out."}}}},{"name":"input_clear","description":"Lets go every key input.set holds.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"input_get_state","description":"The keys input.set holds, by name, and the matrix as rows of bits, a set bit a key down.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"input_press","description":"Presses a PET key for some frames and lets it go, running the PET as it goes.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"key":{"type":"string","description":"The key's name: a character on it (A, 7, \") or RETURN, SPACE, LEFT_SHIFT, RIGHT_SHIFT, RVS, STOP, HOME, DEL, CRSR_DOWN, CRSR_RIGHT, LEFT_ARROW, UP_ARROW."},"shift":{"type":"boolean","description":"Hold the left SHIFT with it; false when left out."},"frames":{"type":"integer","description":"Frames to hold it; 2 when left out. It is then let go for 2."}},"required":["key"]}},{"name":"input_set","description":"Holds a PET key down, or lets it go, until told otherwise. The PET does not run.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"key":{"type":"string","description":"The key's name, as input.press takes it."},"down":{"type":"boolean","description":"Down, or up."}},"required":["key","down"]}},{"name":"input_type","description":"Types a text on the PET's keyboard, a key at a time, held 2 frames and let go 2, running the PET as it goes. Letters in either case are the unshifted keys, which make capitals in the graphics set; \\n is RETURN. In braces: {RETURN}, {CLR}, {HOME}, {DEL}, {INST}, {UP}, {DOWN}, {LEFT}, {RIGHT}, {RVS}, {OFF}, {STOP}, {RUN}, {PI}, or a key with SHIFT, {SHIFT-A}.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string","description":"What to type."},"hold_frames":{"type":"integer","description":"Frames each key is held; 2 when left out."},"gap_frames":{"type":"integer","description":"Frames each key is let go before the next; 2 when left out."}},"required":["text"]}},{"name":"io_get_state","description":"The PIAs' and the VIA's registers, read without side effects, the VIA's timers as they count, and the IRQ line.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"memory_list_regions","description":"The memory regions memory.read and memory.write address, with their sizes.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"memory_read","description":"Reads bytes, without the side effects a read by the 6502 has: by default as the 6502 sees its address space, I/O registers and the bus left floating included; or from a region of memory.list_regions.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte's address in the region."},"size":{"type":"integer","description":"How many bytes, at most 65536."},"region":{"type":"string","description":"CPU when left out; RAM, VIDEO_RAM or one of the ROMs."}},"required":["address","size"]}},{"name":"memory_write","description":"Writes RAM or video RAM as a debugger does: no bus cycle is made and no device runs. The whole range is checked first, so it is written whole or not at all; in CPU addresses it must lie in RAM, $0000-$7FFF, or video RAM, $8000-$87FF.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte's address in the region."},"data_hex":{"type":"string","description":"The bytes, two hex digits each."},"region":{"type":"string","description":"CPU when left out; RAM or VIDEO_RAM."}},"required":["address","data_hex"]}},{"name":"program_load","description":"Puts a .prg into RAM at its load address as BASIC's LOAD does, setting where BASIC's variables begin after it. With run, types RUN for a program at $0401, BASIC's start, and SYS to its first byte for any other, into the keyboard buffer: the PET runs it when it next runs, from READY. Give path or data_hex.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"A .prg file."},"data_hex":{"type":"string","description":"The .prg's bytes, its load address first, two hex digits each."},"run":{"type":"boolean","description":"Run it as well; false when left out."}}}},{"name":"state_list","description":"The state files in the state directory, by name.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"state_load","description":"Restores a state state.save wrote, of a PET with the same ROMs, by this build.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"filename":{"type":"string","description":"The state's file."}},"required":["filename"]}},{"name":"state_save","description":"Writes the whole PET's state to a file: all a run changes, without the ROMs, breakpoints, watchpoints or the trace. A name without a directory is in the state directory.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"filename":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write it."}},"required":["filename"]}},{"name":"video_screen_text","description":"The 25 lines of the screen as text, as the character set on show draws them: letters, digits and punctuation as themselves, graphics as the nearest Unicode character.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"video_screenshot","description":"The last complete picture, the 320 by 200 dots of the 40 by 25 characters, completed where the vertical blank begins: lit dots white, the rest black. Written to path as a PNG, or returned as one.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the PNG; left out, it is returned."}}}}]}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"version\":\"devel\",\"paused\":false,\"running\":false,\"error\":\"no ROM directory is given\"}"}],"isError":false}}
